+There are three ways and all three wait for the same thing: `eciStop` from any thread, answering `eciDataAbort` from the callback, and simply letting the utterance finish and throwing the samples away. Answering `eciDataAbort` is the cheapest, because it is the only one that stops the engine making the samples nobody will hear, and above 11,025 Hz making them is most of what a cancel costs.
 
